<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_32" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:error id="StaffSaveFailure_36" name="Staff account save failed" />
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_32">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_32" name="BPMN-32 | Staff Account Provisioning and Maintenance" processRef="Process_32" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_32" name="Staff Account Provisioning and Maintenance" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-32 and all catalog ownership/reuse rules; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.3 FR-STAFF-01-06; supporting NFR-SEC-02-03,05,08,13, NFR-REL-03,05 and BR-24. Website: index.html loads app/owner-accounts.js M.save/statusChange/find/duplicate, app/session-state.js and app/staff-state.js. Existing docs XMLs reviewed for style/reuse, particularly BPMN-12 and BPMN-31; detailed local validations/failures remain on the main diagram. Scope: authenticated Admin/Owner creates, updates or deactivates a Staff account. Authentication and staff login/session enforcement belong to BPMN-26 and are referenced as precondition/dependent policy, not rerun here. BPMN-27 is customer registration and must not be called to provision Staff. No staff invitation, email verification, password reset, account deletion, configurable role promotion or reactivation is inferred; prototype reactivation is outside this bounded catalog process. Two internal role lanes share sequence flows; no external notification/provider interaction is required, so no message flow or broadcast signal is invented. Input: requested action, allowed staff data, selected account/version for update/deactivate, authenticated administrator and operation identity. Output: new active Staff account linked to creating administrator, updated Staff details, or inactive account denied Staff access; cancellation/rejection/failure preserves prior state. Prototype requires first/last names, valid unique email and an initial password for creation; these are prototype-aligned input examples rather than new SRS-specific password policy. Proposed secure password storage follows NFR-SEC-02, never a claim that browser-only preview hashing is production security. Preserve original creating-administrator association on maintenance. Staff remains restricted to authorized operational functions, including preparing-owner selection/percentages, without financial/customer-management access or automatic owner allocation. Save/account status and effective access state remain consistent; existing inactive-account sessions cannot retain operational authority. Actual sign-in and session lifecycle remain in BPMN-26. No unrelated business records or financial allocations are changed.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_32">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_36_admin" name="Admin/Owner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_36</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
